From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: compact Settings rows on short screens

On a screen under 600 dp tall (the Zinwa Q25's 411 dp square screen)
Android 16's expressive Settings rows are 72 dp cards with 20 dp
corners, so about three fit before scrolling. SettingsLib's theme now
uses compact values there (owner pick from the JL10 review, after
BlackBerry 10): 56 dp rows, 8 dp vertical text padding, 8 dp corners,
an 8 dp gap above a category, and category titles in letter-spaced
small capitals. values-h600dp-v36 keeps Android's own values for every
taller screen, so other devices see no change.

Resources only: three new dimens replace literals in the expressive
preference styles. Settings, SystemUI and every SettingsLib user pick
them up.
---
 .../res/values-h600dp-v36/dimens.xml          | 25 +++++++++++++++++
 .../styles_preference_expressive.xml          | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../SettingsTheme/res/values-v36/dimens.xml   |  9 +++++-
 .../styles_preference_expressive.xml          | 12 ++++++--
 4 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

